      "properties": {
        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "both",
        "summary": "R-1 is a zero-field SMM with dual magnetic relaxation. χmT at 300 K is 55.17 cm3 mol-1 K; after a minimum at 14 K it rises slightly at 2 K, consistent with weak ferromagnetic interaction. AC data under 0 Oe show frequency-dependent χ'/χ'' peaks. Orbach/QTM/Raman fitting gives Ueff = 43.52 K (τ0 = 3.71e-6 s) for the fast relaxation phase and Ueff = 30.91 K (τ0 = 6.90e-5 s) for the slow phase. CD in methanol shows enantiomeric Cotton effects; UV-vis has ligand n-π* and π-π* bands.",
        "measurements": [
          {
            "property_type": "magnetic",
